From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 04:22:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tests: include stdlib.h for _set_fmode in ltcdecode

ltcdecode.c calls _set_fmode() on Windows but only includes fcntl.h.
mingw-w64 declares _set_fmode in stdlib.h, and GCC 14+ treats the
implicit declaration as an error, so `make check` fails to build.
ltcencode.c and example_encode.c already get it via stdlib.h.
---
 tests/ltcdecode.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tests/ltcdecode.c b/tests/ltcdecode.c
index 04e25d3..09b7824 100644
--- a/tests/ltcdecode.c
+++ b/tests/ltcdecode.c
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
 #include <fcntl.h> // for _fmode
+#include <stdlib.h> // for _set_fmode
 #endif
 
 #define BUFFER_SIZE (1024)
